扫描命中行的代码上下文（±25 行窗口，L<n> 为包内原始行号）：
L1: /**
L2:  * memini memory plugin for opencode.
L3:  *
L4:  * Hooks opencode's plugin API so memory is automatic — the model never has to
L5:  * call a tool:
L6:  *   - chat.message: recall memories relevant to the incoming user message and
L7:  *     inject them as a synthetic context part before the turn runs.
L8:  *   - event (session.idle): capture the completed user/assistant turn into
L9:  *     memini once the session goes idle.
L10:  *
L11:  * Talks to memini over REST (/v1/search, /v1/memories), scoped by the
L12:  * X-Memini-Namespace header. Default endpoint http://localhost:8080.
L13:  *
L14:  * Config comes from the plugin options (the [name, options] form in
L15:  * opencode.json), with env-var fallbacks; secrets like MEMINI_API_KEY come
L16:  * from the environment. Namespace and behavioral settings (recall, capture,
L17:  * recall_limit, ...) are additionally cross-checked against the server via
L18:  * POST /v1/handshake — see effectiveConfig() below for the precedence. See
L19:  * the options/env table in ../README.md.
L20:  */
L21: 
